              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سلوانا — silvānā — \"to have (clothes) sewn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "میں نے درزی سے نیا کرتا سلوایا۔ maiṅ ne darzī se nayā kurtā silvāyā. I had a new kurta made by the tailor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے نئی شلوار سلوائی, us ne naī shalvār silvāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سلوانا (silvānā) is the second causative of sīnā, \"to sew\", which CDIAL lists under Sanskrit sīvyati, \"sews\" (CDIAL 13444): to have someone sew."
            }
          ]
        },
